---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="Hermes Mail | Personal email automation"
    description="Hermes Mail is Bruno Farfán Miquel's private, approval-gated email assistant."
    canonicalPath="/hermes-mail/"
>
    <article class="policy-page">
        <div class="container policy-page__inner">
            <nav class="policy-page__nav" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
                <a href="/">bruni.to</a>
                <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
                <span>Hermes Mail</span>
            </nav>

            <header class="policy-hero">
                <p class="eyebrow">Private utility</p>
                <h1>Hermes Mail</h1>
                <p class="policy-hero__lead">
                    A personal email assistant built for deliberate automation:
                    useful access when requested, explicit approval before an
                    action changes a mailbox or sends a message.
                </p>
            </header>

            <div class="policy-grid" aria-label="Hermes Mail overview">
                <section class="policy-card">
                    <p class="policy-card__index" aria-hidden="true">01</p>
                    <h2>What it does</h2>
                    <p>
                        Hermes Mail can search and read connected Gmail
                        accounts, download an attachment when requested, prepare
                        messages, change labels, and move messages to Trash.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section class="policy-card">
                    <p class="policy-card__index" aria-hidden="true">02</p>
                    <h2>How actions are controlled</h2>
                    <p>
                        Sending email and changing mailbox state require a
                        separate, short-lived owner approval. Approved actions
                        are bound to the exact message or operation and execute
                        at most once.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section class="policy-card">
                    <p class="policy-card__index" aria-hidden="true">03</p>
                    <h2>Who it is for</h2>
                    <p>
                        This is a private application operated by Bruno Farfán
                        Miquel for personally controlled or explicitly
                        authorized accounts. It has no public signup or
                        commercial user service.
                    </p>
                </section>
            </div>

            <section class="policy-callout" aria-labelledby="data-title">
                <div>
                    <p class="eyebrow">Data &amp; privacy</p>
                    <h2 id="data-title">Narrow access, clearly described.</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="policy-callout__body">
                    <p>
                        OAuth credentials are kept outside the assistant's
                        direct access. Email content is handled only to perform
                        owner-requested tasks and is never sold or used for
                        advertising.
                    </p>
                    <a class="policy-link" href="/hermes-mail/privacy/">
                        <span>Read the privacy policy</span>
                        <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
                    </a>
                </div>
            </section>

            <p class="policy-contact">
                Questions about Hermes Mail?
                <a href="mailto:info@bruni.to">info@bruni.to</a>
            </p>
        </div>
    </article>
</Layout>
